# msil/utils/ci/det-manifest.py (plan 5.12.12, section 12 'Cross-host
# determinism'; M23), the manifest of CIL objects and archives that the CI's
# determinism job compares across hosts and run-m1-gate.ps1's determinism row
# within the development host: its offline self-test (stand-ins for clang
# and llvm-ar in a temporary directory outside the repository) builds a
# small tree twice from different work directories and compares, checks the
# command lines (relative sources, -fdebug-compilation-dir=., both x86_64
# MSIL triples at each level, -fms-compatibility-version=19.33 on the
# windows-msvc compiles only, so that the triple an object records does not
# depend on the host's MSVC), an edited source, compare's one-sided,
# disjoint and malformed manifests, a work directory inside the repository
# and a failed compile; relative, '/'-separated tool paths run from the root
# (msil-ci.yml's form before M23's fix loop: the stand-ins refuse a relative
# path, and the archiver runs from the work directory); a work directory
# holding a foreign file (refused, the file kept) or only <triple>/
# directories (emptied); a tool that does not start, refused before anything
# is deleted.
# M25 (plan 5.14.3 A2; section 12, 'Plan 5.12.12 amended (determinism
# manifest)'): build also builds the helper archives clang_rt.builtins of
# both triples with build-builtins.py (a stand-in in the self-test), and the
# manifest lists them as <triple>/builtins/<archive> without their stamps
# (18 entries); build-builtins.py gets --build-dir <the directory above the
# tools' bin/> (absolute, also from relative tool paths), --out
# <work>/builtins, both triples and --jobs. The failure paths: an edited
# helper source changes the two helper archives and nothing else; --clang
# and --ar outside one bin/ directory are a usage error before anything is
# deleted; a failed helper archive build writes no manifest.
# RUN: %python %S/../../utils/ci/det-manifest.py --self-test > %t.log 2>&1
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^det-manifest: self-test passed \(0 failure\(s\)\)$" "^ok: two work directories give equal manifests$" "^ok: compare fails on a differing entry$" "^ok: a work directory inside the repository is refused$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: relative '/'-separated tool paths, run from the root, pass the archive step$" "^ok: a work directory holding a foreign file is refused, and the file survives$" "^ok: a work directory holding only <triple>/ directories is emptied and marked$" "^ok: a missing --clang is a usage error before anything is deleted$" "^ok: a missing --ar is a usage error before anything is deleted$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: relative sources and -I, .*, -fms-compatibility-version=19\.33 on every windows-msvc compile and on no linux-gnu one$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: 18 entries \(3 objects and an archive, 2 triples, 2 levels; 2 helper archives\)$" "^ok: the helper archives are listed as <triple>/builtins/<archive>, without their stamps$" "^ok: build-builtins\.py gets --build-dir <the directory above the tools' bin/>, --out <work>/builtins, both triples and --jobs$" "^ok: relative tool paths give build-builtins\.py the absolute build directory$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: build after a helper source edit$" "^ok: an edited helper source differs in the 2 helper archives only$" "^ok: --clang and --ar outside one bin/ directory are a usage error before anything is deleted$" "^ok: a failed helper archive build writes no manifest$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} lacks %t.log "^FAIL: "
